# Example: map, filter, and fold on arrays

These are methods of arrays. The block is a delayed function, evaluated per element.

## Schema

```
Team = [Player]/players
Player = String/name Int/score
```

## Construction

```
[:Team
  [:Array/Player
    ["Ada" 3]
    ["Bob" 0]
    ["Cy" 5]
  ]
]
```

## Methods

```
Team::names = { players.map({ p | p.name }) }

Team::scorers = { players.filter({ p | p.score > 0 }) }

Team::total = { players.fold(0, { acc, p | acc + p.score }) }
```

## Target

```
%main
public static function main():Void {
    var assemblage = teamFactory();
    var helper = new WCHNTHelper();
    trace(assemblage.toConstruction(0, helper));
    trace("names");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(assemblage.names(), 0));
    trace("scorers");
    trace(helper.arrayToConstruction(assemblage.scorers(), 0));
    trace("total");
    trace(assemblage.total());
}
```
